@LP-TEST-UNIVERSAL-AST-CROSS-MODAL @LP-TEST-AST-ROLE-IDENTITY-SEPARATION
Feature: Every digital structure uses one typed universal AST and Merkle DAG

  Scenario: Unrelated modalities share composition laws without flattening structure
    Given a sentence an image region a function body an audio phrase and a model block
    When their declared grammars and codecs lower them into the universal typed AST
    Then every leaf and composition uses the same content identity and trajectory laws
    And modality source role and interpretation remain witnessed dimensions outside node identity

  Scenario: Equal subtrees reuse identity while occurrences retain their paths
    Given one exact subtree occurs in unrelated sources languages and parent structures
    When the complete working set calculates its candidate Merkle DAG
    Then the equal subtree has one content identity and one calculated physicality per recipe
    And every parent role ordinal span source and testimony occurrence remains independently addressable

@LP-TEST-AST-MERKLE-REUSE @LP-TEST-AST-OPAQUE-FLATTENING-REJECTION
Feature: The Merkle DAG is the persistent AST rather than an ETL optimization

  Scenario: A flattened record cannot impersonate the typed tree
    Given a source structure with nested roles order multiplicity ambiguity and an unknown field
    When an implementation emits only an opaque row triple token list or embedding
    Then admission fails unless its receipt exactly reconstructs every required distinction
    And a deliberate opaque-record implementation fails the AST acceptance suite

  Scenario: Partitioning cannot change the persistent tree
    Given the same exact structures as scalar batches partitions and a cross-source working set
    When the canonical recipe and composition engine execute them
    Then identities trajectories AST roots and receipts have identical semantic content
    And repeated subtrees are calculated once per whole working set rather than once per source adapter

@LP-TEST-AST-EXACT-RECOMPOSITION @LP-TEST-RECIPE-DECOMPOSE-RECOMPOSE
Feature: Grammar recipes decompose and recompose exact content

  Scenario: Exact inverse recomposition reproduces the source
    Given a registered grammar provider with nodes fields spans errors and scanner outputs
    And a versioned exact decomposition and inverse recipe
    When the source is lowered to the typed AST and recomposed
    Then the resulting bytes equal the original bytes
    And every concrete node field omission ambiguity error and recovery has an exact disposition

@LP-TEST-RECIPE-STRUCTURAL-TRANSFORMATION @LP-TEST-REALIZATION-PROVENANCE-CLOSURE
Feature: Intentional generation is a receipted AST transformation

  Scenario: Polarity register reference degree and prosody change structurally
    Given the exact witnessed utterance "I don't feel so good Mr Stark"
    And a semantic-act recipe requesting positive polarity emphatic degree informal register resolved given-name address and exclamatory prosody
    When the recipe transforms the typed AST and the English realizer recomposes it
    Then it produces the exact content "I feel fucking great, Tony!"
    And the receipt names every changed role reused subtree reference witness grammar choice and resulting content identity
    But unreceipted string replacement or next-token continuation cannot satisfy the scenario

  Scenario: The same semantic act lowers without an English intermediate
    Given the transformed semantic act and witnessed realization grammars for two unrelated languages and one non-text modality
    When each realizer executes through the same recipe and ISA lifecycle
    Then each output preserves the requested roles evidence and completion obligations
    And no English surface tree becomes the universal semantic plan

@LP-TEST-RECIPE-ISA-COMPILATION @LP-TEST-RECIPE-OPAQUE-CALLBACK-REJECTION
Feature: Every recipe compiles through the common typed ISA

  Scenario: A recipe preflights as one complete program
    Given a versioned recipe with typed inputs outputs grammar dependencies epochs authority resources effects vectors and completion
    When the recipe compiler lowers it
    Then one vector-first ISA program and immutable context are validated before output or mutation
    And native PostgreSQL SQL and Csharp routes use generated bindings to the same semantic implementation

  Scenario: A private recipe callback is rejected
    Given a source adapter parser codec template or model handler containing an unregistered semantic callback
    When framework admission inspects the operation
    Then execution is rejected before the callback can emit content testimony or effects
    And a deliberate callback-bypass mutant fails the recipe acceptance suite

@LP-TEST-RECIPE-LOSS-AND-INVERSE @LP-TEST-RECIPE-VERSION-HISTORY
Feature: Recipe loss and evolution remain explicit

  Scenario: Lossy transformation cannot claim exact reconstruction
    Given a recipe that discards a source distinction required by a declared consumer
    When it attempts to publish an exact result
    Then publication fails with the discarded distinction and affected consumer in the receipt

  Scenario: A semantic recipe change creates a new coordinate
    Given a previously activated recipe and historical receipts
    When lowering validation or recomposition semantics change
    Then a new authority release namespace version coordinate and fingerprint are appended
    And prior content testimony calculations and receipts remain reproducible under the old version

@LP-TEST-GENERIC-SEMANTIC-SINGLE-OWNER @LP-TEST-GENERIC-PROVIDER-SUBSTITUTION
Feature: Generic providers vary mechanism without varying meaning

  Scenario: Unrelated grammar and persistence providers share one lifecycle
    Given two grammar providers and two persistence providers satisfying the same typed contracts
    When each combination executes the same recipe program
    Then AST output order evidence completion and receipt semantics remain identical
    And only provider identity resource use physical plan and measured performance may differ

@LP-TEST-GENERIC-SOURCE-BRANCH-REJECTION @LP-TEST-GENERIC-SCALAR-BATCH-ROUTE-PARITY
Feature: A source cannot create another engine

  Scenario: Source modality language and model branches cannot own semantics
    Given unrelated sources with different serializations and witness dimensions
    When their recipes execute as scalar vector parallel direct-native and PostgreSQL routes
    Then every route uses the common AST recipe ISA working-set provider sink and receipt spine
    And a source-named semantic dispatcher or one-item implementation fails acceptance
